  ],
  "text": "A bat can find a wire thinner than a human hair, in total darkness, at full speed. It is not seeing in the dark. There is nothing down there to see. It shouts. Then it listens very carefully to what comes back. The delay tells it distance. The change in the sound tells it shape. Do that fast enough, often enough, and what you have is a picture. Which started an arms race. And the moths have won some of it. Some moths jam the sonar with ultrasonic clicks of their own. Others grew scales that soak the sound up. Acoustically invisible. A battle you cannot hear has been running over your head for fifty million years. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
